# One finding ID per line (CVE, GHSA, AVD-DS-*, secret rule, license).
# Optional expiry suffix: ' exp:YYYY-MM-DD'. Audited suppressions carry a
# statement in docs/operations.md.
#
# Every entry carries an `exp:` expiry; when a waiver lapses, the finding
# becomes a gate failure again and must be re-evaluated (bump the carrying
# dependency, or renew with justification). Waivers apply to the publish-time
# Trivy gates (publish-mech-images.yml) and the weekly audit
# (container-audit.yml). Each finding below was enumerated from a scan of
# mech-server@sha256:8129ed13... on 2026-10-03; see docs/operations.md
# "Container hardening" for the full analysis.
#
# --- SDK-borne Python packages in /agent-server/.venv (mech-server) -------
# The server image is assembled by the upstream OpenHands agent-server build
# (sdk:openhands-agent-server/v1.50.1) on top of mech-tools; these versions
# come from upstream's dependency resolution, not this repo's uv.lock (the
# mech-tools scan is clean). pypdf, urllib3, virtualenv, wheel, setuptools,
# msgpack, and jaraco.context findings clear on the next openhands-sdk bump —
# tracked in scripts/dependency_update_deferrals.json.
